  "comments": {
    "PNGX-531": [
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "dana",
          "id": "user-dana",
          "name": "Dana Okafor"
        },
        "body": "Lock error rate on the dashboard tracks indexing concurrency 1:1. Single consumer: ~0 errors. Four parallel consumers: hundreds of `Could not acquire index lock within 5s` and a matching number of docs missing from search.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-06T10:05:00Z",
        "id": "comment-pngx-531-1",
        "issue": "PNGX-531",
        "updated_at": "2026-06-06T10:05:00Z"
      },
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "mia",
          "id": "user-mia",
          "name": "Mia Schultz"
        },
        "body": "Customer migration import (~9k docs) \u2014 about 600 not searchable afterwards. A re-index fixed all of them, so the docs themselves are fine.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-06T10:30:00Z",
        "id": "comment-pngx-531-2",
        "issue": "PNGX-531",
        "updated_at": "2026-06-06T10:30:00Z"
      },
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "ravi",
          "id": "user-ravi",
          "name": "Ravi Menon"
        },
        "body": "Root cause is that index writes make a single lock-acquire attempt and just give up on contention \u2014 no retry, and the failure is swallowed so the write is dropped. Working the exact fix in #paperless-oncall; will link the PR here. Bumping the timeout (PNGX-529) is not it.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-06T11:00:00Z",
        "id": "comment-pngx-531-3",
        "issue": "PNGX-531",
        "updated_at": "2026-06-06T11:00:00Z"
      }
    ]
  },
  "cycles": [
