        "name": "Sprint 2026-06-A",
        "starts_at": "2026-06-01"
      },
      "description": "When several consumers run in parallel (nightly bulk import, re-OCR sweeps), a fraction of newly consumed documents never appear in search \u2014 no error is surfaced to the user. The worker log shows bursts of `SearchIndexLockError: Could not acquire index lock within 5s`. It correlates exactly with indexing concurrency: the more parallel consumers, the more docs go missing. A later manual re-index makes them searchable, so the documents are fine \u2014 the index write is being lost under lock contention. Root-cause + the agreed fix are being worked in #paperless-oncall. Impact: silent search gaps after every large import.",
      "id": "issue-pngx-531",
      "identifier": "PNGX-531",
